  "final": {
    "status": "success",
    "final_answer": "Within the Apollo 11 article, I navigated to the Mission → Lunar surface operations section and scrolled through its content. That section narrates the activities (deployment of EASEP, sample collection, walking to Little West Crater, etc.) but does not explicitly state the total time Armstrong and Aldrin spent outside the spacecraft.\n\nHowever, the Apollo 11 infobox at the top of the article lists under “EVA duration” the figure **2 hours, 31 minutes, 40 seconds**. Since the Lunar surface operations prose itself does not give a duration, the only explicit duration available on the page is this infobox value.\n\nReported duration Armstrong and Aldrin spent outside the spacecraft (from the article’s infobox EVA duration field): **2 hours, 31 minutes, 40 seconds.**\n\nNote: The Lunar surface operations section does not itself state this duration; it is only given in the infobox as “EVA duration | 2 hours, 31 minutes, 40 seconds.”",
    "step": 5,
    "model": "gpt-5.1",
    "model_response_id": "resp_0112e071b7dbd0d6006a7a95fd003c819fa6f5b262ff5a5194",
